To fix this, we can automatically assign a default tenant (or handle an unset tenant by defaulting it or checking how tests expect it) or update the guard to default to a test tenant or fallback value if none is set, or initialize with a default value. Looking at the test, it calls `guard.sanitize_and_bind_query` immediately after instantiating `MultiTenantGuard`, so `self.tenant_id` should either default to a safe value or be automatically set.

